(2285702, 311372, 20956, '<td valign="top">Enter your comment here, and then cast javascript: do_vote(5)<br/> 5 your vote...</td>', 'Enter your comment here, and then cast javascript: do_vote(5) 5 your vote...', '2006-04-04 07:53:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285711, 310880, 30364, '<td valign="top">A beautiful image that uses a real-world object to create, or at least to suggest, something else.  I suppose some might argue that it''s not technically ''abstract'' in art terms, in that it''s representational.  But it is representational of something other than what it actually is, so I figure that qualifies.  And the thing that it represents is a state, rather than an object.  In any case, more than 90% of the entries in this challenge are not even vaguely abstract, so you''re way ahead!  I applaud the vision, the elegance and the sympathetic title.  9.</td>', 'A beautiful image that uses a real-world object to create, or at least to suggest, something else.  I suppose some might argue that it''s not technically ''abstract'' in art terms, in that it''s representational.  But it is representational of something other than what it actually is, so I figure that qualifies.  And the thing that it represents is a state, rather than an object.  In any case, more than 90% of the entries in this challenge are not even vaguely abstract, so you''re way ahead!  I applaud the vision, the elegance and the sympathetic title.  9.', '2006-04-04 08:00:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285713, 312587, 55099, '<td valign="top">A foot...(heel(?))</td>', 'A foot...(heel(?))', '2006-04-04 08:05:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285716, 312875, 30364, '<td valign="top">Unusual that one of the handful of other worthwhile images in this challenge has the same title, and involves the very same idea.  I honestly can''t separate the two "Flow" images, so I have to offer the same comment and the same score:<br/> <br/>A beautiful image that uses a real-world object to create, or at least to suggest, something else.  I suppose some might argue that it''s not technically ''abstract'' in art terms, in that it''s representational.  But it is representational of something other than what it actually is, so I figure that qualifies.  And the thing that it represents is a state, rather than an object.  In any case, more than 90% of the entries in this challenge are not even vaguely abstract, so you''re way ahead!  I applaud the vision, the elegance and the sympathetic title.  9.<br/> <br/>Sorry I can''t be more original, but at least I''m fair!</td>', 'Unusual that one of the handful of other worthwhile images in this challenge has the same title, and involves the very same idea.  I honestly can''t separate the two "Flow" images, so I have to offer the same comment and the same score: A beautiful image that uses a real-world object to create, or at least to suggest, something else.  I suppose some might argue that it''s not technically ''abstract'' in art terms, in that it''s representational.  But it is representational of something other than what it actually is, so I figure that qualifies.  And the thing that it represents is a state, rather than an object.  In any case, more than 90% of the entries in this challenge are not even vaguely abstract, so you''re way ahead!  I applaud the vision, the elegance and the sympathetic title.  9. Sorry I can''t be more original, but at least I''m fair!', '2006-04-04 08:07:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285719, 311729, 30364, '<td valign="top">It''s a very challenging photograph.  Most of what I see is reflected, I think.  The colours are well done, and unify the chaos just enough.  I feel I should be able to resolve this image, but fortunately I can''t.  8.</td>', 'It''s a very challenging photograph.  Most of what I see is reflected, I think.  The colours are well done, and unify the chaos just enough.  I feel I should be able to resolve this image, but fortunately I can''t.  8.', '2006-04-04 08:12:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285740, 310852, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is fascinating.  It is probably just a hole in a bit of metal (razor blade? metal ruler?), but that''s irrelevant.  What is so appealing about it is the fact that it suggests a resolution, but never quite delivers it.  The most compelling thought is celestial.  A planet against a meteor shower?  A moon against a mega-planet?  Or maybe it''s something very small; at the sub-atomic level?  Whatever, it is an attractive and absorbing image.  I like the title, too; I feel I almost understand it, but then I don''t.  8.</td>', 'This is fascinating.  It is probably just a hole in a bit of metal (razor blade? metal ruler?), but that''s irrelevant.  What is so appealing about it is the fact that it suggests a resolution, but never quite delivers it.  The most compelling thought is celestial.  A planet against a meteor shower?  A moon against a mega-planet?  Or maybe it''s something very small; at the sub-atomic level?  Whatever, it is an attractive and absorbing image.  I like the title, too; I feel I almost understand it, but then I don''t.  8.', '2006-04-04 08:32:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285751, 313222, 30364, '<td valign="top">This image establishes an idea that presumably has nothing to do with its subject''s actual identity.  It is literally representational, and so maybe not strictly abstract, but its impact is certainly at least largely figurative and that''s near enough for me!  8.</td>', 'This image establishes an idea that presumably has nothing to do with its subject''s actual identity.  It is literally representational, and so maybe not strictly abstract, but its impact is certainly at least largely figurative and that''s near enough for me!  8.', '2006-04-04 08:44:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285760, 310862, 25355, '<td valign="top">I can''t easily identify this at 43rd glance. Nice colours, though.</td>', 'I can''t easily identify this at 43rd glance. Nice colours, though.', '2006-04-04 08:48:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2285773, 311646, 30364, '<td valign="top">My only 10.  I love the elegance of the two curves.  I love the beautiful, subtle tonal gradient.  Most of all, I love the sympathetic distillation of the subject; the way you have isolated and captured its essence without having to represent it literally, or at least entirely.   It''s perhaps not technically abstract, but I don''t technically care.  Bravo!</td>', 'My only 10.  I love the elegance of the two curves.  I love the beautiful, subtle tonal gradient.  Most of all, I love the sympathetic distillation of the subject; the way you have isolated and captured its essence without having to represent it literally, or at least entirely.   It''s perhaps not technically abstract, but I don''t technically care.  Bravo!', '2006-04-04 08:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
