(2290530, 312163, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC.  Glad to see you jumping in and playing.  <br/> <br/>YOur image.  First of all, I liked it.  Good colors and a lively  composition.  <br/> <br/>I am going to suggest a couple of changes to the composition though.  (And please remember all this is just my opinion)  First, you might consider using a colorful background, or white or black.  The gray is just a little bland.  Or you might consider cropping into the colored area removing the background all together.   <br/> <br/>Then, even though you know it is a macro shot, there isn''t scale to give the voter a clue that it is indeed a tiny area.  (I have difficulty learning this,myself)  So some of our more technically minded voters probably worried about the DNMC aspect.  <br/> <br/>But, still it is a bright, vibrant image and one you should like a lot.  I certainly do.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work, and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-05 20:12:52.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Welcome to DPC.  Glad to see you jumping in and playing.   YOur image.  First of all, I liked it.  Good colors and a lively  composition.   I am going to suggest a couple of changes to the composition though.  (And please remember all this is just my opinion)  First, you might consider using a colorful background, or white or black.  The gray is just a little bland.  Or you might consider cropping into the colored area removing the background all together.    Then, even though you know it is a macro shot, there isn''t scale to give the voter a clue that it is indeed a tiny area.  (I have difficulty learning this,myself)  So some of our more technically minded voters probably worried about the DNMC aspect.   But, still it is a bright, vibrant image and one you should like a lot.  I certainly do. Keep up the good work, and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC.', '2006-04-05 21:07:11.000000', '2006-04-05 21:12:52.000000', 0),
