(2291279, 312153, 33505, '<td valign="top">I guess I am new to the dpchallenge game -- I actually <i>added</i> noise to make it look more high-speed artistic something or other. I thought it gave it a nice feel. Well, I think I''m moving SLIGHTLY up in the rankings, so that''s good. And I''m glad people liked the idea. I''ll keep working on it.  :-)</td>', 'I guess I am new to the dpchallenge game -- I actually added noise to make it look more high-speed artistic something or other. I thought it gave it a nice feel. Well, I think I''m moving SLIGHTLY up in the rankings, so that''s good. And I''m glad people liked the idea. I''ll keep working on it.  :-)', '2006-04-06 02:56:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2291367, 311503, 48228, '<td valign="top">I am just been blown away with the interest this image has received, as I now have 45 comments, and 6 favorites..... Thank you all so very much, as you have really made my day.....</td>', 'I am just been blown away with the interest this image has received, as I now have 45 comments, and 6 favorites..... Thank you all so very much, as you have really made my day.....', '2006-04-06 04:43:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2291401, 312956, 50715, '<td valign="top">Sorry, I didn''t get to comment during the voting.<br/> <br/>I was one of those who voted you 3. The technical aspects are quite good, the only possible problem is the washed-out highlights, but this is pretty minor. However, the image was just to ho-hum for me.  For an abstract macro to create interest for me, there needs to be an interesting interplay of colour and/or shapes and/or lines and/or textures. The only one of these that your photo could be said to have is textures (colour is primarily middlish grey, shape is almost an amorphous blob with no strong shape or lines), and even the texture of the scratches and dents or the word is not <i>that</i> interesting visually.<br/> <br/>A looser crop (to get more of the shape) might have helped - would probably need some changes to the lighting though. A tighter crop to about 1/6 of the photo in the top left corner (taking in the straight lines in the corner, plus cropping through the word so you get only some of the curves) could have been a more interesting composition.<br/> <br/>I also felt the white border didn''t really add anything in this particular image.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps!</td>', 'Sorry, I didn''t get to comment during the voting. I was one of those who voted you 3. The technical aspects are quite good, the only possible problem is the washed-out highlights, but this is pretty minor. However, the image was just to ho-hum for me.  For an abstract macro to create interest for me, there needs to be an interesting interplay of colour and/or shapes and/or lines and/or textures. The only one of these that your photo could be said to have is textures (colour is primarily middlish grey, shape is almost an amorphous blob with no strong shape or lines), and even the texture of the scratches and dents or the word is not that interesting visually. A looser crop (to get more of the shape) might have helped - would probably need some changes to the lighting though. A tighter crop to about 1/6 of the photo in the top left corner (taking in the straight lines in the corner, plus cropping through the word so you get only some of the curves) could have been a more interesting composition. I also felt the white border didn''t really add anything in this particular image. I hope this helps!', '2006-04-06 05:25:25.000000', NULL, 0),
