(2296429, 311961, 49447, '<td valign="top">Thank you for your comments.  Not sure what caused the graininess or noise.  There was no digital enlargement, the 640 pixel length was 1/3 the total of the original photo.  Still new to all this and appreciate the constructive criticism.<br/> <br/>These were stamens of the Bourgainvillea plant, taken while I was in Florida last week.  They looked like new "baby chick" legs to me, therefore the title.<br/> <br/>Thanks,  Henry<br/> <br/>edited to add reason for title.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-07 22:15:55.</i></td>', 'Thank you for your comments.  Not sure what caused the graininess or noise.  There was no digital enlargement, the 640 pixel length was 1/3 the total of the original photo.  Still new to all this and appreciate the constructive criticism. These were stamens of the Bourgainvillea plant, taken while I was in Florida last week.  They looked like new "baby chick" legs to me, therefore the title. Thanks,  Henry edited to add reason for title.', '2006-04-07 23:13:45.000000', '2006-04-07 23:15:55.000000', 0),
